        "attr": "Times & Seasons (times_and_seasons:times_and_seasons_1839_1846_1840_december_vol_02_no_04)"
      },
      {
        "text": "\"\u2019The fools of the earth desire to be clad in fine raiment, and to feel\nfor a moment the glory of earthly power, but to those who have once seen\nthe light which proceeds from true wisdom, riches and honour are as\ndust, the shouts of men as the hum of insects, and the kingdoms of earth\nas ant-heaps. ",
        "speaker": "",
        "source": "HoC",
        "date": "",
        "ref": "",
